<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gherardo da Camino</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1240–<a href="/years/1306">1306</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gherardo da Camino was lord of Treviso from 1283 to 1306, captain-general of the city after the fall of the da Romano family. His court welcomed troubadours and poets, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a> praised him in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/purgatorio">Purgatorio</a> as the good Gherardo, an example of courtesy. His son Rizzardo succeeded him but was murdered in 1312.</p></div>
